WWW::Crawl4AI (unreleased, 0.007, commit 3eaac25 "Refuse redirects and name status, method and path in errors") builds its LWP agent with max_redirect => 0: a 3xx is reported as an api error naming status, method and path.

Net::Async::HTTP follows GET/HEAD redirects by default (max_redirects 3). So on the async path job_status (GET /crawl/job/{id}) and health (GET /health) follow a 3xx while the sync facade fails. The redirected request is rebuilt without the Authorization header, so no bearer-token leak, but the Result/error diverges from sync.

Fix: pass max_redirects => 0 in _do_request_with_retry (http->do_request), so the 3xx response reaches the shared parse_* and raises the same error as sync. Regression test: scripted HTTP returning 302 + Location for job_status → Future fails type=api, status_code 302; health → 0. Requires the parser from WWW::Crawl4AI 0.007 for the exact message; bump the cpanfile minimum only if the test depends on it (a dep pinned ahead of CPAN is not a blocker in this family). Update POD/skill net-async-crawl4ai-core if the transport contract wording changes.

